ALL OF THE SYSTEM'S FAILURES, WE

00:19:24.363 --> 00:19:26.899
HAVE TO STOP THIS NARRATIVE THAT

00:19:26.965 --> 00:19:30.369
CRIMINAL JUSTICE REFORM IS JUST

00:19:30.435 --> 00:19:31.603
A CODE WORD FOR LAWLESSNESS AND

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:33.805
LACK OF ACCOUNTABILITY. WE HAVE

00:19:33.872 --> 00:19:35.607
TOOLS WITHIN THE PENAL CODE TO

00:19:35.674 --> 00:19:37.776
HOLD FOLKS ACCOUNTABLE IN THIS

00:19:37.843 --> 00:19:39.811
STATE FOR COMMITTING CRIME. WE

00:19:39.878 --> 00:19:40.812
HAVE AGENCIES THAT ARE

00:19:40.879 --> 00:19:41.947
POSITIONED TO DO THAT, BUT WE

00:19:42.014 --> 00:19:43.081
HAVE A COMMUNITY BASED

00:19:43.148 --> 00:19:44.249
INFRASTRUCTURE THAT WE HAVE TO

00:19:44.316 --> 00:19:46.785
CONTINUE TO INVEST IN. IF WE

00:19:46.852 --> 00:19:47.953
WANT SAFETY TO BE ACHIEVED IN

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.821
THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA. THANK

00:19:49.888 --> 00:19:53.258
YOU. THANK YOU, CASEY. THANK

00:19:53.325 --> 00:19:54.326
YOU. SENATOR. GOOD MORNING. MY

00:19:54.393 --> 00:19:58.130
NAME IS CASEY WARMOTH, AND I AM

00:19:58.196 --> 00:20:00.399
THE CHIEF OF RESEARCH WITH THE

00:20:00.465 --> 00:20:01.567
BOARD OF STATE AND COMMUNITY

00:20:01.633 --> 00:20:04.169
CORRECTIONS. I AM HAPPY TO HAVE

00:20:04.236 --> 00:20:05.270
THE OPPORTUNITY TO SHARE SOME

00:20:05.337 --> 00:20:07.239
POSITIVE INFORMATION ABOUT THE

00:20:07.306 --> 00:20:10.709
PROP 47 GRANT PROGRAM, WHICH IS

00:20:10.776 --> 00:20:13.645
ADMINISTERED BY THE BSC AS

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:14.646
REQUIRED BY THE BALLOT

00:20:14.713 --> 00:20:17.049
INITIATIVE. THE GRANT FUNDS ARE

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:18.116
AWARDED TO PUBLIC AGENCIES TO

00:20:18.183 --> 00:20:20.252
PROVIDE MENTAL HEALTH SERVICES,

00:20:20.319 --> 00:20:23.355
SUBSTANCE USE DISORDER TREATMENT

00:20:23.422 --> 00:20:24.323
SERVICES AND DIVERSION PROGRAMS

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:27.793
FOR PEOPLE WHO ARE IN THE

00:20:27.859 --> 00:20:28.293
CRIMINAL JUSTICE SYSTEM.

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:30.362
ADDITIONALLY LEGISLATION

00:20:30.429 --> 00:20:31.363
REQUIRES THAT THE GRANTS ARE

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:34.132
AWARDED COMPETITIVELY, SPECIFIES

00:20:34.199 --> 00:20:35.233
THAT FUNDS MAY SERVE BOTH ADULT

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:40.939
AND JUVENILES, AND ALSO ALLOWS

00:20:41.006 --> 00:20:42.140
FOR THE FUNDS TO BE USED FOR

00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:44.743
HOUSING RELATED ASSISTANCE AND

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:45.877
OTHER COMMUNITY BASED SUPPORTIVE

00:20:45.944 --> 00:20:50.949
SERVICES. THE BSC FURTHER

00:20:51.016 --> 00:20:52.084
REQUIRES THAT AT LEAST 50% OF

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:53.785
THE FUNDS MADE AVAILABLE TO THE

00:20:53.852 --> 00:20:54.853
GRANTEES ARE PASSED THROUGH TO

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.489
COMMUNITY BASED SERVICE

00:20:57.556 --> 00:20:58.557
PROVIDERS. THE EVALUATION OF THE

00:20:58.624 --> 00:21:01.727
PROP 47 COHORT TWO GRANT PROGRAM

00:21:01.793 --> 00:21:05.797
HIGHLIGHTS HOW THE 92 MILLION IN

00:21:05.864 --> 00:21:07.466
FUNDING THAT WAS PROVIDED TO 21

00:21:07.532 --> 00:21:11.136
GRANTEES BENEFITED CALIFORNIA

00:21:11.203 --> 00:21:13.505
FOR THE GRANT PERIOD BEGAN IN

00:21:13.572 --> 00:21:16.808
AUGUST 2019 AND ENDED IN MAY OF

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:20.479
2023. DURING THIS TIME, GRANTEES

00:21:20.545 --> 00:21:22.981
SPENT OVER $81 MILLION, OF WHICH

00:21:23.048 --> 00:21:24.816
64 MILLION WAS PASSED THROUGH TO

00:21:24.883 --> 00:21:26.218
COMMUNITY BASED SERVICE

00:21:26.284 --> 00:21:27.152
PROVIDERS. THROUGH THE GRANT

00:21:27.219 --> 00:21:30.088
FUNDED PROJECTS, MORE THAN

00:21:30.155 --> 00:21:33.291
21,000 PEOPLE RECEIVED MENTAL

00:21:33.358 --> 00:21:34.393
HEALTH OR SUBSTANCE USE DISORDER

00:21:34.459 --> 00:21:37.262
TREATMENT OR WERE DIVERTED FROM

00:21:37.329 --> 00:21:38.330
THE CRIMINAL JUSTICE SYSTEM

00:21:38.397 --> 00:21:40.432
PROGRAM PARTICIPANTS ALSO

00:21:40.499 --> 00:21:41.366
RECEIVED OTHER SUPPORTIVE

00:21:41.433 --> 00:21:43.902
SERVICES, INCLUDING CASE

00:21:43.969 --> 00:21:47.606
MANAGEMENT, LEGAL HOUSING, AND

00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:48.640
EMPLOYMENT SERVICES. AT THE END

00:21:48.707 --> 00:21:53.245
OF THE GRANT PERIOD, 22% OF

00:21:53.311 --> 00:21:54.212
PARTICIPANTS WERE STILL

00:21:54.279 --> 00:21:56.348
RECEIVING SERVICES AND 32% OF

00:21:56.415 --> 00:21:59.484
PARTICIPANTS HAD SUCCESSFULLY

00:21:59.551 --> 00:22:02.654
COMPLETED PROGRAM REQUIREMENTS

00:22:02.721 --> 00:22:03.655
FOR THE EVALUATION. THREE

00:22:03.722 --> 00:22:06.525
OUTCOME MEASURES WERE EXAMINED

00:22:06.591 --> 00:22:07.025
RECIDIVISM, HOUSING AND

00:22:07.092 --> 00:22:10.195
EMPLOYMENT. FOCUSING ON

00:22:10.262 --> 00:22:13.231
RECIDIVISM FIRST, POSITIVE

00:22:13.298 --> 00:22:14.366
OUTCOMES WERE ACHIEVED FOR THIS

00:22:14.433 --> 00:22:16.768
EVALUATION. RECIDIVISM WAS

00:22:16.835 --> 00:22:18.503
DEFINED AS THE CONVICTION OF A

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:20.672
MISDEMEANOR OR FELONY AFTER

00:22:20.739 --> 00:22:23.775
PROGRAM ENROLLMENT. THIS DOES

00:22:23.842 --> 00:22:24.743
DEVIATE FROM THE USUAL

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:27.412
DEFINITION, WHICH IS CONVICTION

00:22:27.479 --> 00:22:29.047
WITHIN THREE YEARS OF RELEASE

00:22:29.114 --> 00:22:31.116
FROM CUSTODY OR BEING PLACED ON

00:22:31.183 --> 00:22:33.985
SUPERVISION. THIS MODIFICATION

00:22:34.052 --> 00:22:35.187
WAS NECESSARY FOR THE EVALUATION

00:22:35.253 --> 00:22:37.556
TO ACCOMMODATE NOT ONLY THE

00:22:37.622 --> 00:22:40.625
GRANT TERMS, BUT ALSO THAT THE

00:22:40.692 --> 00:22:41.727
PARTICIPANTS HAVE A VARIETY OF

00:22:41.793 --> 00:22:44.429
RELEASE STATUSES AND SUPERVISION

00:22:44.496 --> 00:22:48.033
STATUS FOR THE PARTICIPATION FOR

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:49.067
WHICH RECIDIVISM DATA WERE

00:22:49.134 --> 00:22:51.536
AVAILABLE. 51.3% WERE CONVICTED

00:22:51.603 --> 00:22:54.606
OF A NEW MISDEMEANOR OR FELONY.

00:22:54.673 --> 00:22:57.976
THIS RATE IS SUBSTANTIALLY LOWER

00:22:58.043 --> 00:22:58.944
THAN OTHER REPORTED STATEWIDE

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:01.413
RECIDIVISM ESTIMATES, WHICH

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:07.119
RANGE FROM 35 TO 45. IN ADDITION

00:23:07.185 --> 00:23:08.220
TO THE OVERALL RECIDIVISM RATE,

00:23:08.286 --> 00:23:10.322
THE EVALUATION EXPLORED

00:23:10.388 --> 00:23:11.356
RECIDIVISM BY A VARIETY OF

00:23:11.423 --> 00:23:16.261
FACTORS. THE RECIDIVISM RATE WAS

00:23:16.328 --> 00:23:17.262
11% FOR PARTICIPANTS WHO

00:23:17.329 --> 00:23:19.664
IDENTIFIED AS BLACK OR AFRICAN

00:23:19.731 --> 00:23:23.201
AMERICAN, COMPARED TO 12 TO 17%

00:23:23.268 --> 00:23:24.369
FOR OTHER RACE OR ETHNICITY

00:23:24.436 --> 00:23:28.340
GROUPS. THE RECIDIVISM RATE WAS

00:23:28.406 --> 00:23:29.441
12% FOR PARTICIPANTS WHO WERE

00:23:29.508 --> 00:23:31.543
EMPLOYED EITHER PART TIME OR

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:33.945
FULL TIME, COMPARED TO 15% FOR

00:23:34.012 --> 00:23:35.180
THOSE WHO WERE UNEMPLOYED. AND

00:23:35.247 --> 00:23:37.649
FINALLY, THE RECIDIVISM RATE WAS

00:23:37.716 --> 00:23:39.484
11% FOR THOSE WHO WERE LIVING

00:23:39.551 --> 00:23:41.319
INDEPENDENTLY, COMPARED TO 18%

00:23:41.386 --> 00:23:44.456
FOR THOSE WHO WERE HOMELESS.

00:23:44.523 --> 00:23:48.059
FOCUSING ON HOUSING OUTCOMES,

00:23:48.126 --> 00:23:51.496
THIS OUTCOME WAS EVALUATED FOR

00:23:51.563 --> 00:23:52.497
THE 6000 PARTICIPANTS WHO

00:23:52.564 --> 00:23:55.967
IDENTIFIED HOUSING AS A GOAL FOR

00:23:56.034 --> 00:23:56.968
THOSE WHO COMPLETED PROGRAM

00:23:57.035 --> 00:23:58.904
REQUIREMENTS, HOMELESSNESS WAS

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:01.840
REDUCED BY 60% COMPARED TO

00:24:01.907 --> 00:24:04.042
PROGRAM ENROLLMENT.

00:24:04.109 --> 00:24:05.010
ADDITIONALLY, THE PROPORTION OF

00:24:05.076 --> 00:24:07.579
PEOPLE LIVING INDEPENDENTLY

00:24:07.646 --> 00:24:08.580
NEARLY DOUBLED, FOCUSING ON

00:24:08.647 --> 00:24:11.616
EMPLOYMENT OUTCOMES. THIS

00:24:11.683 --> 00:24:14.486
OUTCOME WAS ALSO EVALUATED FOR

00:24:14.553 --> 00:24:15.420
THE APPROXIMATELY 6000

00:24:15.487 --> 00:24:18.156
PARTICIPANTS WHO IDENTIFIED

00:24:18.223 --> 00:24:19.324
EMPLOYMENT AS A GOAL FOR THOSE

00:24:19.391 --> 00:24:21.393
WHO COMPLETED PROGRAM

00:24:21.459 --> 00:24:22.260
REQUIREMENTS. UNEMPLOYMENT WAS

00:24:22.327 --> 00:24:25.497
REDUCED BY 50, AGAIN RELATIVE TO

00:24:25.564 --> 00:24:28.233
PROGRAM ENROLLMENT. MOST

00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:29.267
EMPLOYMENT GAINS WERE IN PART

00:24:29.334 --> 00:24:32.137
TIME EMPLOYMENT, ALTHOUGH THE

00:24:32.204 --> 00:24:33.205
PROPORTION OF PARTICIPANTS WHO

00:24:33.271 --> 00:24:35.273
WERE EMPLOYED FULL TIME ALSO

00:24:35.340 --> 00:24:38.276
INCREASED. IN SUMMARY, THE

00:24:38.343 --> 00:24:39.344
BENEFITS OF THE COHORT TWO

00:24:39.411 --> 00:24:41.012
PROPOSITION 47 GRANT PROGRAM

00:24:41.079 --> 00:24:44.049
INCLUDED LOWER RECIDIVISM RATES

00:24:44.115 --> 00:24:45.116
COMPARED TO OTHER STATEWIDE

00:24:45.183 --> 00:24:47.919
RECIDIVIST ESTIMATES AND A

00:24:47.986 --> 00:24:50.989
REDUCTION IN HOMELESSNESS AND

00:24:51.056 --> 00:24:52.090
UNEMPLOYMENT FOR THE THOUSANDS

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:54.659
OF PARTICIPANTS WHO MADE

00:24:54.726 --> 00:24:55.727
POSITIVE LIFE CHANGES. THE

00:24:55.794 --> 00:24:58.396
BENEFITS ARE IMMEASURABLE. THANK

00:24:58.463 --> 00:25:01.833
YOU. AND THIS CONCLUDES MY

